    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, thanks. I'm also a bit worried about the 'random chance' part you mentioned. In my discussion section, I need to address the possibility that these results are just due to error or noise in the data. How should I scientifically frame the concept of 'uncertainty' or 'stochastic error' so it doesn't sound like I'm just guessing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
